+/*
+ * U880 native display bring-up switches (msm.u880_dbg, writable at runtime). Bits:
+ * 0x1 both INTF timing engines, 0x2 prefetch 129 lines, 0x4 DSI FIFO recovery, 0x8 PLL OUTDIV bit 2, 0x10 PLL SSC,
+ * 0x20 PHY1 own timings, 0x40 panel ON+PPS before video, 0x80 PLL SYSTEM_MUXES + PHY1 CLK_CFG0, 0x100 DSI CLK_EN off,
+ * 0x200 uke single-CTL split flush, 0x400 vendor PHY strength values, 0x800 lane-3/clock-lane vendor values,
+ * 0x1000 DSC without SPLIT_PANEL (Android), 0x2000 PHY resync FIFO toggle + CLK_EN_SEL clear before video,
+ * 0x4000 restore bootloader-only INTF bits, 0x8000 start slave+master timing engines back to back.
+ * 0x40000 vendor hardware DSI command broadcast (slave armed, master triggers), 0x80000 C-PHY resync FIFO toggle
+ * (CLK_EN_SEL kept) + DSI soft reset after the link clocks run.
+ * 0x100000 unicast DSI commands per link (panel sends ON+PPS to DSI0 then DSI1; no sync broadcast).
+ *   + 0x200000 only DSI0 gets the sequence, + 0x400000 only DSI1.
+ * 0x1000000 DSI CLKOUT_TIMING=0, 0x8000000 TPG fifo bit off, 0x2000000 DSI VBIF_CTRL=7 (HANGS), 0x4000000 TRIG_CTRL block-dma bit off (Android parity),
+ * 0x10000000 PPS pic_width = 800 (per link) instead of 1600 (wrong: upstream uses the full width), 0x20000000 DCS 0x9d 0x01 after the PPS (NT36532),
+ * 0x40000000 DCS status reads per link at the end of panel prepare (logged as "dcsread linkN reg ..."; unicast mode also logs 0x0a/0x0f after ON and after PPS),
+ * 0x80000000 unicast order: link 1 first, 0x800000 phased unicast (ON on both links, then PPS on both).
+ */
+extern unsigned int u880_dbg;
+/*
+ * msm.u880_dbg2:
+ * 0x1 bind DSC_n to the other pingpong (DSC_0<-PP_1, DSC_1<-PP_0)
+ * 0x2 lock-step dual-IC panel init: send init regs to both links, 0x11 sleep-out on both links back-to-back,
+ *     single msleep(100) while both ICs wake up together, then 0x29 display-on on both, then PPS on both
+ * 0x4 60 Hz panel refresh mode (lower C-PHY link rate to test DSI0 signal integrity)
+ * 0x8 disable SSPP multirect parallel (allocate 2 separate SSPP pipes for left/right halves like Android)
